# Example drop-in override: /etc/caddy/moshpit.d/app.chovy.hacker.caddy
#
# Any file matching /etc/caddy/moshpit.d/*.caddy is imported INTO the site
# block in the template, so it must contain directives that are valid inside
# a site block — not a site block of its own.
#
# This one routes app.chovy.hacker to port 3000 instead of the 8080 default.
# `handle` blocks are ordered by matcher specificity, so this host match wins
# over the template's catch-all no matter where the import lands.

# @svc-app host app.chovy.hacker
# handle @svc-app {
# 	reverse_proxy localhost:3000
# }
#
# Matcher names must be unique across the whole site block — the template
# already uses `@app` for its example, so pick your own (e.g. `@svc-app`).
# To override a different subdomain, copy the two lines above, uncomment,
# and change the name and port. One pair per override. Then:
#
# 	sudo systemctl reload caddy      # or: caddy reload
